## Folder Structure Reference

```
AGENTS.md                     AI-facing master instructions (workflow, rules, gotchas)
README.md                     This guide
.ai/
├── knowledge-base.md         Canonical domain, architecture, and module reference (project-owned)
├── governance/               Coding standards, SCM workflow, security, SQL rules, WCAG patterns
├── behavior/                 STOP/FLAG/PROCEED decision rules, per-ticket-type risk posture, ADA workflow
├── templates/                Commit-message and pull-request templates
├── data-dictionary/          DB schema and stored-procedure reference (only if generated for this project)
└── .toolkit-sync-state.json  Bookkeeping file for /sync-toolkit (hidden file) — do not edit or delete
.github/
├── copilot-instructions.md   Always-on guardrails Copilot reads for every request
├── agents/                   Ticket Processor (ticket-to-PR) and Domain Engineer (implementation/review)
├── prompts/                  Slash commands: fix-ticket, auto-fix, implement, pr-review, sync-toolkit
└── skills/                   Reusable implementation patterns (patterns/SKILL.md)
data-dictionary-tooling/      SQL export queries used to build .ai/data-dictionary/ (may not apply to your database engine)
```

`.ai/knowledge-base.md` and `.ai/data-dictionary/` belong to this project — they are generated from
its own code and documents and are never changed by toolkit updates.

**What is `.ai/.toolkit-sync-state.json`?** It is the toolkit's bookkeeping file (hidden, because
its name starts with a dot). `/sync-toolkit` uses it to remember, for each toolkit-managed file,
which toolkit version that file has caught up to, when it was last synced and what the result was.
It holds no copies of toolkit files: when you update, the original files of the recorded versions
are read from the toolkit clone's git history (so the clone must still have those versions'
tags), which is what lets updates merge changes without overwriting your customizations. Deleting
it makes the next sync treat this project as not installed; never hand-edit it — after reconciling
a file by hand, record it with `/sync-toolkit --source <path> --mark-reconciled <manifest-path>`
instead. Commit it with the rest of `.ai/`.

The toolkit's generators (the commands that build `.ai/knowledge-base.md`, the governance files,
and so on) are **not** installed in this project; they are read straight from your toolkit
clone when needed — see "Re-running a single generator" below.

